<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo April trade gap $58 mln vs $113 mln in March.</title>
<headline>Yugo April trade gap $58 mln vs $113 mln in March.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported on Wednesday the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	April 97   March 97     April 96</p>
<p> Exports million USD  184.0	151.0	   155.0</p>
<p> Imports		  242.0	264.0	   278.0</p>
<p> Balance		 - 58.0     -113.0	  -123.0</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO APRIL)</p>
<p> Exports million USD  677.0	454.0	   484.0</p>
<p> Imports		1,330.0	947.0	 1,036.0</p>
<p> Balance		 -653.0     -493.0	  -552.0</p>
<p>NOTES -- April year-on-year imports fell 12.9 percent while exports rose 19.3 percent, the report said.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-April imports were up 28.4 percent and exports rose 39.9 percent against the same period 1996.</p>
<p>Data refer to Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Yugoslavia ended 1996 with a $2.26 billion trade gap.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
